.\" AintScrape man page
.TH AINTSCRAPE 1 "August 2026" "aintscrape 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aintscrape \- modem IP rotator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aintscrape
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AintScrape
forces a new public IP address by rotating the IP on a 4G/5G modem
via its management API. It handles Linux routing and exposes rotation as a
CLI tool or HTTP endpoint.
.PP
Built for CGNAT environments where the ISP hands out fresh IPs on modem
reconnect. Currently supports Huawei HiLink gateways; run
.B aintscrape drivers
to see all supported modems.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B rotate
Run a single IP rotation and print old/new IPs.
.TP
.B hard-rotate
Full hardware modem reboot/reset on all interfaces.
.TP
.B fix
Force re-enable mobile data and reconnect the interface.
Skips if the interface already has an IP. Useful after a
cancelled rotation or Ctrl+C left the modem with data off.
.TP
.B serve
Start the HTTP rotation service (foreground).
.TP
.B version
Print version and exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Path to configuration file (default: /etc/aintscrape/config.yaml).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read from a YAML file. See
.B /etc/aintscrape/config.yaml
for the default configuration and
.B config.example.yaml
for all available options.
.PP
The configuration file search order is:
.RS 4
.IP 1. 4
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
command-line argument
.IP 2. 4
.I /etc/aintscrape/config.yaml
.IP 3. 4
.I ./.env
(legacy fallback)
.RE
.PP
Real environment variables always take precedence over the file.
.SH HTTP API
When running in
.B serve
mode, the following endpoints are available:
.TP
.B POST /rotate
Trigger an IP rotation. Returns JSON with old_ip, new_ip, and rotated fields.
.TP
.B GET /health
Health check endpoint. Returns {"status": "ok"}.
.PP
If
.B auth_token
is set in the configuration, the
.B X-Auth-Token
header is required for the /rotate endpoint.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/aintscrape/config.yaml
Configuration file.
.TP
.I /lib/systemd/system/aintscrape.service
Systemd service unit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Rotate the IP once:
.RS 4
.B aintscrape rotate
.RE
.PP
Re-enable mobile data after a failed rotation:
.RS 4
.B aintscrape fix
.RE
.PP
Start the HTTP service:
.RS 4
.B aintscrape serve
.RE
.PP
Trigger rotation via HTTP:
.RS 4
.B curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/rotate
.RE
.PP
Use a custom config:
.RS 4
.B aintscrape --config /path/to/config.yaml rotate
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Configuration error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR ip (8),
.BR sysctl (8)
